"cost_per_unit\": 4.611070832129442, \"effective_lea", "advisory_context": true, "prompt_injection_flagged": false}, {"citation_id": "C3", "source_id": "component-shortage-playbook", "source_type": "playbook", "title": "Component Shortage Response Playbook", "chunk_id": "component-shortage-playbook-1", "score": 0.72725296, "text_excerpt": "# Component Shortage Response Playbook **Trigger.** A supplier declares allocation, a lane's effective capacity drops toward zero, or inbound receipts fall materially below the plan for a critical component. ## Immediate assessment 1. Identify which finished goods depend on the constrained component via the BOM. 2. Classify the constraint: is the limit **supply availability** (nothing to order) or **inventory policy** (stock on hand mis-positioned)? These require different responses and should be stated plainly to planners. 3. Quantify unavoidable lost sales: demand that cannot be met because supply, not policy, is gating. Do not present recoverable and unrecoverable shortfall as the same nu", "advisory_context": true, "prompt_injection_flagged": false}, {"citation_id": "C4", "source_id": "component-shortage-playbook", "source_type": "playbook", "title": "Component Shortage Response Playbook", "chunk_id": "component-shortage-playbook-2", "score": 0.7042879, "text_excerpt": "order does not increase delivered units and inflates cancellation, holding, and expedite cost. - Do not claim an inventory-policy change \"recovered\" sales that were lost to zero supply. Under a genuine zero-supply shock the tuned policy may only be able to reduce cost, not restore fill. ## Reporting - Report the benchmark-selected plan's objective, fill rate, and days of inventory as computed by the optimizer. Narrative rationale is advisory and must not restate or override those numbers.", "advisory_context": true, "prompt_injection_flagged": false}, {"citation_id": "C5", "source_id": "planner-notes", "source_type": "planner_note", "title": "Benchmark planner notes", "chunk_id": "planner-notes-1", "score": 0.6912019, "text_excerpt": "Planner note. The benchmark-selected approach is classical. PPO outcome: lost_to_classical. Objective tie across approaches: False. The rationale should distinguish baseline, tuned classical, and PPO based on the benchmark result, not based on generic claims.", "advisory_context": true, "prompt_injection_flagged": false}], "retrieval": {"backend": "qdrant", "collection": "helix_sco_rag_component-shortage-shock", "top_k": 5, "embedded_chunks": 19, "embedding_model": "nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5", "embedding_dimension": 768}, "prompt_injection_flags": [], "llm_profile": {"name": "rag_rationale_llm", "scenario": "component-shortage-shock", "wall_clock_seconds": 13.403652, "peak_process_rss_mb": 1640.09375, "allocation_rate_gbps_proxy": 0.000183, "cpu_utilization_percent": 2.8, "gpu_utilization_percent": null, "gpu_memory_used_mb": null, "gpu_metrics_status": "unavailable: GB10 unified-memory nvidia-smi query reports N/A inside this stack", "gpu_start": {"gpu_utilization_percent": null, "gpu_memory_used_mb": null, "gpu_metrics_status": "unavailable: GB10 unified-memory nvidia-smi query reports N/A inside this stack"}, "model": "nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B-FP8", "completion_tokens": 644, "prompt_tokens": 2156, "total_tokens": 2800, "tokens_per_second": 48.046607}, "llm_usage": {"prompt_tokens": 2156, "total_tokens": 2800, "completion_tokens": 644, "prompt_tokens_details": null}, "artifacts": {"rationale_path": "/app/benchmark/component-shortage-shock-rag-advisory-rationale.json"}}}